          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: This observation made on January 11, 2014 at 4:50 PM, along with the associated photograph, exhibits all the characteristics of an airplane contrail observed during sunset. See for this regard an information from GEIPAN: airplane contrails. The FlightRadar site log shows intense aerial activity within the witness's field of view: several planes could have produced this condensation trail. The weather log indicates a north wind with excellent visibility of 60 km. The observed trail is likely at 100 or 120 km, visible due to its altitude (10,000 m) and especially the lighting conditions from the setting sun. It is probably due to these excellent weather conditions, and from an unusual perspective, that the witness was surprised by this rather mundane phenomenon. GEIPAN classifies this case as \"A\": observation of an airplane condensation trail. For information: comets are only visible at night, as their trail is dimly lit.",
